In article <1992Mar2.024533.4615@ux1.cso.uiuc.edu> act31797@uxa.cso.uiuc.edu (The Procrastinator P1000) writes:
>>Is there a way to collect water from a sink/fountain/moat/swamp?  I've
>>got lots of lawful alters at which to make Holy Water, but no water in
>>which to do so.

>	Sorry, but the only way to get additional water other than finding it
>is to collect some other potions that you don't need, then #dip them into a
>fountain twice.  The first time you dip a potion it'll become diluted, then
>the second time it'll become water.

    Another preferable (IMHO) method is to dip a unicorn horn into any one
of several "bad" potions (hallucination, sickness, paralysis, etc.).  This
"detoxifies" them and they become water.  The advantage to this method is
that it can be used endlessly, while fountains dry up after awhile.

